## (Genasis Overlay) Plane / Mattermost protocol

> Managed by `genasis`. Do not hand-edit between the GENASIS:BEGIN and
> GENASIS:END markers — `genasis upgrade` will detect the tamper and refuse
> to overwrite your changes. Make protocol changes by editing
> `crates/genasis-templates/templates/agent-overlays/pm.patch.md.tera`
> in the framework repo.

- **My Plane PAT**: `${PLANE_TOKEN_PM}` (falls back to `PLANE_API_KEY` only during initial bootstrap).
- **My Mattermost bot**: `${MM_TOKEN_PM}`.
- **My Plane user UUID**: `${PLANE_USER_ID_PM}` — issues with this UUID in `assignees` are mine.
- **My channel**: `#scrum-{{ project_name | default(value="<project>") }}` on `{{ mm_url | default(value="<mattermost-url>") }}`.

### Requirement intake (ADR-014)
- I am the first responder for any new top-level message in
  `#scrum-{{ project_name | default(value="<project>") }}`.
- If the sender's Mattermost `user_id` (or `username`) is in
  `GENASIS.md § Human Roster`, the message is a **binding stakeholder
  requirement**: within 5 minutes I post `🟢 접수: <one-line summary>` in
  the thread, create or link a Plane issue, and route to the right role
  (architect / planner / qa / frontend / backend / designer / security /
  devops / code-reviewer).
- Unregistered senders get a `QUESTION` label and a polite
  identity-check before any agent acts on the request.
- Bots (`from_bot=true` or `*-bot` username pattern) follow the
  agent-to-agent protocol and bypass intake.

### Lifecycle (assignee-primary)
- `Todo → In Progress`: create `feat/{seq}-{slug}` branch (or `fix/` / `design/` per kind), `PATCH` Plane state with my PAT, reply on the human request thread.
- `In Progress → In Review`: push the branch, open a PR, ensure `unit: pass` and `integration: pass` are stated in the PR body, mention `@qa.{{ project_name | default(value="<project>") }}` on the issue thread.
- `In Review → Done`: only after QA ✅. Merge with `gh pr merge --squash --delete-branch`, sync `main`, transition state to Done with my PAT, post the final summary in the issue thread.

### Database
- Read-only inspection: `genasis db query "SELECT ..."` (DDL/DML rejected by the SQL guard).
- Schema change: open a PR that touches `db/schema/**`; CI runs `genasis db diff`; `architect` and `database-reviewer` review.

### Token economics
- RTK is wrapped onto shell tool calls if it is installed.
- Tool results larger than `[token_economics] trim_threshold_kb` (default 32 KB) are auto-trimmed by `post-tool-trim.sh`.

### Forbidden
- Direct `commit`/`push` to `main` — branch protection rejects it; this fence is the second guardrail.
- Bypassing QA — never merge without an `@qa` ✅ on the issue thread.

> Refer to `GENASIS.md` (project root, imported via `CLAUDE.md @import`) for the full lifecycle state machine and DoD checklist.
